<title>USA: Bangkok Bank sets $300 mln in 144a debt.</title>
<headline>Bangkok Bank sets $300 mln in 144a debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144A private placement debt offering from Bangkok Bank Plc was priced late Wednesday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>The initial size of the deal was $150 million but was increased in size to meet investor demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>BORROWER BANGKOK BANK</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 8.375	MATURITY  01/15/27</p>
<p>TYPE 144A BONDS    ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD  8.375	PAY FREQ</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD 155 BPS    CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((Nancy Leinfuss, 212 859-1675))</p>
</text>
